Z||000000||ezsurf||09-02-2001||03:04 PM||||I'm finally getting the interior back in my car.  However, I have one part that I don't remember where it goes.  The Pontiac (Helm) manual doesn't show where it goes either. I need some help. Anyone recognize this?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sp02_004.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||ezsurf||09-02-2001||03:07 PM||||Sorry the image is so big, this is my first attempt at posting a photo. - At least no one will need their glasses. lol||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||09-02-2001||03:07 PM||||Console brace just below the tape/radio cover.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mach10||09-02-2001||03:16 PM||||Yep. It mounts parrallel with the radio face, just in front of the shifter console section.<P>Here we have a perfect example of Murphys law:<BR>"Take apart a Fiero and reassemble enough times, you will have enough leftover parts to assemble 2 complete Fieros. Neither of which will work"||||reg||7
Z||000004||ezsurf||09-02-2001||03:30 PM||||Thanks for the info.  I'll check it out when I get home.  I hope no one is confusing the brace that goes right in front of the shifter.  That piece is only about half the lenght of this one, and does not have the 90 degree bends on each end.  I have that piece and I know where it goes.  Also, does anyone know if this piece only goes with the stock radio?  My stock radio was fried, so I may not be able to attach this piece anymore.  If this piece is still attachable, I'm thinking it goes underneath the black plastic console skeleton.  Does this sound right, or am I confused?||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||09-02-2001||08:09 PM||||i thought you were always supposed to have parts left over  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>my problem is i put every part in a container as i take them off and i still lose something. That Murphy guy is everywhere.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ezsurf||09-03-2001||01:42 PM||||Thanks for the input.  I got it figured out now.  I took the interior apart over a year ago.  I also put all the parts in a compartmented storage box.  I expected the Pontiac manual to show  where everything went.  I really didn't expect it to have so many omissions.  If I ever tear a car down to this stage again, I'm going to throughly document the disassembly with both digital and regular photographs.  I've learned a lot rebuilding this car, most of it the hard way.||||reg||14
